    "narrative": "As we navigate this late-October slate, our offensive output for the Austin Waves is constrained by a light schedule, leaving us with a concentrated look at **Liam Hicks** and **Brayan Rocchio**. **Liam Hicks** emerges as our primary play, carrying a 51.1 efficiency score against Armstrong. His placement in the #3 hole provides the requisite volume to anchor our production, and while Armstrong isn't a total pushover, the positive adjustment for **Liam Hicks**\u2014driven by his recent form and a favorable platoon dynamic\u2014makes him a high-floor start today. Conversely, **Brayan Rocchio** sits at the lower threshold of our starting criteria with a 40.9 score. The matchup against Peralta, F is daunting, and being buried at the bottom of the order severely dilutes his R and RBI potential, leaving him as a marginal start solely for his proximity to our roster caps.\n\nOur bench remains stagnant today due to a league-wide off-day for the bulk of our core, including **Kyle Tucker**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, all of whom are inactive. We continue to monitor the status of **Luis Robert Jr.**, who remains sidelined on the IL, preventing any consideration for his elite speed profile. With the rest of our roster\u2014from **Jackson Merrill** and **Andy Pages** to high-upside prospects like **Henry Bolte** and **Franklin Arias**\u2014not scheduled to play, we are effectively in a holding pattern. The risk today is minimal regarding weather, but the lack of depth in the confirmed lineups means we are strictly playing the hand dealt by the schedule. We maintain a defensive posture with **Brayan Rocchio**, prioritizing the preservation of our game caps over chasing marginal production in what is otherwise a quiet day for the Austin Waves.",
